<Project>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      MinVer derives the version from the git tag (see Directory.Build.props). Build-time only:
      Directory.Build.props references it with PrivateAssets="all", so it appears in no nuspec.
    -->
    <PackageVersion Include="MinVer" Version="7.0.0" />

    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.DevServer" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Server" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.FluentUI.AspNetCore.Components" Version="4.14.4" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Proxies" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational.Specification.Tests" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Specification.Tests" Version="10.0.0" />
    <!--
      10.0.9, not 10.0.0. This entry is a TRANSITIVE PIN, not a dependency of the product:
      CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled makes it bind every transitive reference in the repo,
      and EF Core's SQLite package reaches Microsoft.Extensions.Logging 10.0.9, which floors this
      at 10.0.9. Pinned lower, the restore fails with NU1109 in the test and sample projects.
      Raising it changes no declared dependency of InfoCarrier.Core, which references only
      Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore and Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational.

      CORRECTED 2026-08-17 (M8-19), and only the last sentence was wrong. It IS a declared
      dependency of the *package*: transitive pinning promotes a pin into the nuspec, so
      InfoCarrier.Core.10.0.0-preview.1 declares Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection >= 10.0.9
      even though no csproj references it. Left as it is — the floor is real (EF Core's SQLite
      package reaches it), and consumers of an EF provider acquire that package anyway — but it is
      recorded because a dependency nobody chose is exactly what nobody looks for. Turning
      CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled off for the packable projects is the alternative, and
      it reintroduces the NU1109 this pin exists to prevent.
    -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="10.0.9" />
    <!--
      TRANSITIVE PINS THAT CLOSE NU1903 ADVISORIES. Neither package is referenced by anything in
      this repository, and neither reaches either product: `dotnet list package` with the
      `vulnerable` switch reports InfoCarrier.Core and InfoCarrier.Core.AspNetCore clean. They
      arrive behind EF Core's own providers, so the fix is a version floor rather than a
      suppression. Nothing here is being accepted as a risk.

      SQLitePCLRaw 2.1.11 to 2.1.13 (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q, high). Reached through
      Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.Core by Northwind.Server and both test projects. The four packages are
      one family and ship in lockstep, so pinning `lib.e_sqlite3` alone would leave `core`,
      `bundle_` and `provider_` a version behind it.

      System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.0 to 10.0.11 (EIGHT high advisories: GHSA-23rf-6693-g89p,
      GHSA-37gx-xxp4-5rgx, GHSA-6588-8gv4-xfgh, GHSA-8q5v-6pqq-x66h, GHSA-cvvh-rhrc-wg4q,
      GHSA-g8r8-53c2-pm3f, GHSA-mmjf-rqrv-855v, GHSA-w3x6-4m5h-cxqf). Reached ONLY by
      InfoCarrier.Core.FunctionalTests, through Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer and
      Microsoft.Data.SqlClient. 10.0.x rather than a 9.0.x patch because everything targets net10.0.
    -->
    <PackageVersion Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3" Version="2.1.13" />
    <PackageVersion Include="SQLitePCLRaw.core" Version="2.1.13" />
    <PackageVersion Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3" Version="2.1.13" />
    <PackageVersion Include="SQLitePCLRaw.provider.e_sqlite3" Version="2.1.13" />
    <PackageVersion Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.11" />

    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.12.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.0.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="System.Text.Json" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="coverlet.collector" Version="6.0.2" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
